| ShortSummary    = In 1931 [[New York City]], several [[Chronicoms (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Chronicoms]] steal the faces of three police officers and kill a contact from a local speakeasy. [[S.H.I.E.L.D. (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|S.H.I.E.L.D.]] agent [[Jemma Simmons]] introduces Director [[Alphonso Mackenzie (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Alphonso "Mack" Mackenzie]] and agent [[Daisy Johnson (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Daisy Johnson]] to an [[Life Model Decoy (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Life Model Decoy]] (LMD) version of [[Phil Coulson]], who struggles with his existence and the amount of information uploaded into him. Daisy and [[Deke Shaw]] investigate the faceless officers and are attacked by the Chronicoms, but they overpower one and take him back to the ''Zephyr''. Coulson and Mack investigate the speakeasy and meet its owner, [[Ernest Koenig|Ernest "Hazard" Koenig]], who reveals that the police officers are providing security for a function in honor of Gov. [[Franklin D. Roosevelt]]. Simmons overloads the Chronicom's mind, forcing it to reveal their actual target: Koenig's employee [[Wilfred Malick|Wilfred "Freddy" Malick]], father of future [[Hydra (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Hydra]] leader [[Gideon Malick]]. The team rescues Freddy from the Chronicoms and realize they have to save Hydra to ensure S.H.I.E.L.D.'s future. On the ''Zephyr'', the Chronicom [[Enoch (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Enoch]], an ally of S.H.I.E.L.D., helps heal Agent [[Melinda May]].
| LineColor       = 73CDE2
}}
