| ShortSummary    = The Lighthouse automatically fires missiles at the ''Zephyr'', damaging the time drive. While Deke, Simmons, and Enoch repair it, Deke discovers that Simmons has a memory implant that blocks her knowledge of [[Leo Fitz]]'s location while retaining information on time travel. Nathaniel experiments on Daisy and transfers her powers to himself, but he is overwhelmed by them as they destroy the building he is in, allowing Sousa to get Daisy back to the ''Zephyr''. May uses her powers to identify undercover Chronicoms while she and Coulson rescue General [[Rick Stoner (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Rick Stoner]], and Coulson finds the Chronicoms' ship. He speaks with their predictor, [[Sibyl (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Sibyl]], before blowing up the ship with himself and many of the Chronicoms in it. Mack and Yo-Yo discover that Mack's parents are already dead and being impersonated by Chronicoms, forcing Mack to throw them from the [[Quinjet]]. The ''Zephyr'' jumps to 1982, and Mack steps out to mourn. Deke checks on him, but they are stranded when the ''Zephyr'' suddenly jumps through time.
| LineColor       = 73CDE2
}}
